 "text": "The slot holds the head `discriminant + sentences` for `tinyclip-8m-16` (shrinkage 0.03, species_com, gamma 1), fitted on `images/alachua-2025 (two thirds of val)`, with 5911 species rows, and a bias a row. Every photo's vector (`images/alachua-2025.wasm-int8-per-channel`) went through `tools/fusion/fuse.py`, the reference of the page's arithmetic, with the slot's own files as the page reads them (half-precision rows). Settings: rule `product`, t_kind 50, w_kind 0.3, alpha_prior 0.5. On 565 tuning photos (the third of val kept for tuning) the thresholds came out as name_at never (no level reached nine in ten) and offer_at 0.24. On the 4197 test photos the kind of eye is right for 77.6% (76.4 to 78.9); the top species is right for 25.3% (24.0 to 26.6) and is among the first five for 45.5% (44.0 to 47.0). `person` was said for 0.05% of these photos and `none` for 0.10%; the set holds neither. The top species from fuse.py differs from a direct matrix computation on the same files for 0 photos. The kinds head is `kind phrases`. With kind_at 0.58 (set on wildlife tuning photos alone, because the extra set's vectors were not published for this model), the page asserts a kind for 52.4% (50.9 to 54.0) of the wildlife test photos and is right for 94.3% (93.3 to 95.3) of those; for the 47.6% (46.0 to 49.1) where it is not sure, the true kind is among its three likeliest for 89.0% (87.6 to 90.4). The slot needs: species.bias_url (build 7 of the page); fusion.kind_at (the build of the page that has the answer `not sure`).",
